    "case_id": "686",
    "case_summary": "A 2-year-old girl was admitted with a history of repeated episodes of embolic stroke. The patient had been undergoing ambulatory rehabilitation and required frequent pump exchange. Past medical history included paracorporeal continuous-flow LVAD implantation. Patient's weight was 12 kg and height was 82 cm.\n\nInitial physical examination details were not explicitly provided in the case report.\n\n- Imaging Studies:    1. Computed Tomography (Pre-transplant):       - Maximal transverse diameter of left hemithorax: 9.4 cm        2. Serial Post-operative CT scans:       Image Title: Post-operative CT with image reconstruction       Image Description (POD 7): Heart deviated the tracheobronchial tree to the right, compressed left bronchus, and occupied almost the entire left hemithorax              Image Description (POD 123): Decreased size of the cardiac allograft, relieved compression of left bronchus, improved expansion of left lung              Image Description (POD 214): Further size remodeling of the cardiac allograft and only mild residual compression of the left bronchus        3. Echocardiography:       - Serial measurements of LVEF       - Left ventricular mass index       - TAPSE       - TRPG",
